 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`; `data/seed.json` has one key
+per role.
+
+- `viewer` may only read (`GET`).
+- `cook` may also cook (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager` may do everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a
+known key without permission answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every non-`GET` request made with a known key writes an audit entry
+`{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`, whatever its outcome (requests
+refused with 401 are not recorded). `GET /audit` lists the entries newest
+first and is for managers only.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
